Interesting - Neither of us has it completely right.  A monster
including a pet will pick up any artifact.  A monster including a pet
will wield the first artifact weapon in its item list that it can wield.
In effect it will ignore cross aligned artifacts and when it picks up a
new artifact whether it gets wielded depends on the location in the
carried item list.  The item list is not populated in a predictable. 
When an item is no longer carried it leaves a blank in the list.  When
an item is picked up it goes to the first open slot which might be a
blank and might be at the end.

So a monster can pick up an artifact and wield it immendiately or could
pick up an artifact and keep it, or pick up an artifact and eventually
drop it for lack of use.

